Select the ROCm component categories you want to install. You can select
multiple components for a customized installation.

[H1]Core Component Categories:

[H2]core
    Core ROCm components required for basic ROCm functionality.
    Includes base libraries and runtime components.

[H2]core-dev
    Core development components for building ROCm applications.
    Includes development headers and libraries.

[H2]dev-tools
    Developer tools for ROCm application development and debugging.
    Includes profilers, debuggers, and development utilities.

[H2]opencl
    OpenCL runtime support for ROCm.
    Enables OpenCL applications to run on AMD GPUs.

[H2]core-sdk (Select All Core)
    Complete ROCm SDK with all core components above.
    Selecting this option automatically includes core, core-dev, dev-tools,
    and opencl. Recommended for full ROCm development environment.

[H1]Expansion Component Categories:

[H2]hpc-sdk (HPC SDK)
    AMD ROCm HPC SDK provides high-performance computing libraries and
    tools for AMD Instinct GPUs. Selecting this option automatically
    includes hipTensor and rocAlution libraries.

[H2]hiptensor
    hipTensor is a high-performance HIP C++ library for accelerating tensor
    primitives. It leverages specialized GPU matrix cores on the latest AMD
    discrete GPUs. The hipTensor API is designed to be portable with other
    similar libraries, letting other library users easily migrate to the
    AMD platform.

[H2]rocalution
    rocALUTION is a sparse linear algebra library that can be used to explore
    fine-grained parallelism on top of the ROCm platform runtime and toolchains.
    Based on C++ and HIP, rocALUTION provides a portable, generic, and flexible
    design that allows seamless integration with other scientific software
    packages.

[H1]Usage:

You can select individual components for a customized installation, or
select 'core-sdk' to install all core components at once, or select
'hpc-sdk' to install HPC libraries.

The 'core' component is recommended as the minimum installation.

Use Space or Enter to select/deselect items.
Press <DONE> when finished to return to the ROCm Options menu.
